# CYP-670 — Relay JVM launch args, SINGLE SOURCE for the macOS LaunchDaemon wrapper (deploy/launchd/relay-run.sh).
#
# The relay previously launched with ZERO JVM args (`relayRun` set none — the same "zero hardening" class as the old
# `gatewayRun`, before CYP-667). It runs on Netty → it needs the JFR guard (CYP-206/225 NoClassDefFoundError
# FreeChunkEvent on a stripped JDK); a bounded heap gives a knowable ceiling. One arg per line; `#`/blank ignored.
#
# ★ D2 (PO-ratified INTO CYP-670): the relay carries Noise-ENCRYPTED frames, but its heap can still hold connection
#   metadata / peer-handshake material BEFORE encryption → "marginal" ≠ "zero". Uniform hardening with the hub/gateway
#   (zero-downside, behavior-neutral): the FULL set + `Core=0` in the plist.
-Dio.netty.jfr.enabled=false
-XX:MaxRAMPercentage=75.0
-XX:-HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:-CreateCoredumpOnCrash
